    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Could you expand on the contingency protocols specifically? Like, if a shipment gets stuck at a customs port for 24 hours due to a paperwork error, what specific steps should the local team take to ensure the integrity of the shipment isn't compromised during that delay?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If a shipment is held at customs for an extended period, the local team must immediately initiate \"Quarantine Protocol Gamma,\" which involves transferring the shipment to a validated, monitored cold storage unit *on-site* at the customs facility, if possible. If on-site validated storage isn't available, the next step is to engage a pre-vetted, certified third-party logistics (3PL) provider who specializes in emergency cold chain storage. Crucially, they must continuously monitor the temperature logger and log the deviation frequency, documenting every temperature reading hourly, not just every few hours. This documentation is vital for proving due diligence should the vaccine viability be questioned later.",
